==English==

===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|la|custōdia||a keeping, watch, guard, prison}}, from {{m|la|custōs||a keeper, watchman, guard}}. {{doublet|en|custode}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkʌstədiː/}} ([[w:Estuary English|Estuary English]])
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-custody.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{homophones|en|custardy}} (in some dialects)

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|-|+}}

# The legal right to [[take care of]] something or somebody, especially children.
#: {{ux|en|The court awarded '''custody''' to the child's father.}}
#: {{ux|en|The mother gained '''custody''' of the children.}}
# Temporary [[possession]] or care of somebody else's property.
#: {{ux|en|I couldn't pay the bill and now my passport is in '''custody''' of the hotel management.}}
# The state of being [[imprison]]ed or [[detain]]ed, usually pending a [[trial]].
#: {{ux|en|He was mistreated while in police '''custody'''.}}
# {{lb|en|Roman Catholicism}} An area under the [[jurisdiction]] of a [[custos]] within the [[order|Order]] of Friars Minor.
#: {{ux|en|The '''Custody''' of the Holy Land includes the monasteries of Bethlehem, Nazareth, and Jerusalem.}}

